E. Proof target sharpened
  HYP-2438 can be split into two marked-support lemmas:
    L1 finite ladder: if Q41 has a witness, the band-ladder closes directly.
    L2 concentrated support: if Q41 is blocked, the marked set-cover ledger has
       either a universal blocker or repeated high-load cover runners; that marked
       runner should feed Bprime(any runner) or an owner-private deletion opening.
  This is a proof obligation, not yet a proof.  The new invariant is the minimum
  blocker support per q plus cross-q cover load; it is the address coordinate
  missing from raw Res_27/Q search.
